+# Data export
+
+A tenant admin requests an export from Settings → Data. The request creates an
+`export_jobs` row; the worker picks it up within 30 seconds.
+
+## Flow
+
+1. `POST /api/export` creates a `pending` job scoped to the caller's tenant.
+2. The worker claims up to 25 pending jobs per batch and writes one CSV per
+   job to object storage.
+3. `GET /api/export?id=…` returns a signed, 15-minute download URL once the
+   job is `done`.
+
+## Isolation
+
+Ordinary request traffic runs with `app.tenant_id` pinned, so the RLS policies
+on `export_jobs` and `export_audit` restrict every statement to the caller's
+tenant. The worker is the exception: it must see pending jobs across all
+tenants, so it announces itself with `app.elevated_read` before the claim
+query.
